rentImage` was already incremented.\n\nLooking at the condition `mClicked == mClickedFilter`, I can trace through different scenarios: if nothing's changed, both are false and navigation proceeds. If only a filter is applied, both are false and navigation is allowed—which seems intentional, assuming unfiltered images don't need saving. If a filter is applied and save is clicked, then `mClicked` becomes true while `mClickedFilter` stays true, so the condition holds and navigation works.\n\nBut there's a problem: if the user clicks save, then navigates, `mClicked` gets reset to false while `mClickedFilter` remains true, creating a mismatch. This inconsistency is the actual bug.\n\nThe solution is to add logic that sets `mClickedFilter = true` after a successful save, ensuring the flags stay in sync. I need to be careful about where this goes since `saveCurrentImage()` can be called from multiple places, but looking at the code, it's only invoked from `saveC()`, so updating the flag there should cover all cases. The fix involves adding `mClickedFilter = true` after the save operation completes, right after `mPhotoEditor.saveAsFile()` is called. This ensures both flags are in sync whenever an image is saved, whether through brush or filter changes. I'll apply this change now.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
